{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/scribe-neutral", "sessionId": "9f2c1d84-6b70-4a15-9c3e-2d8b7a614f03", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": null, "type": "user", "uuid": "86b04a92-84b7-4769-9496-a5c874a38270", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:12:52.295261+00:00", "permissionMode": "acceptEdits", "promptSource": "sdk", "promptId": "700d594d-970b-487f-89e4-3f04157b0dba", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "Different documents need different rules, and I should not have to edit the source to convert one properly. Make that configurable, and tell me what the conversion actually did to each document."}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/scribe-neutral", "sessionId": "9f2c1d84-6b70-4a15-9c3e-2d8b7a614f03", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "86b04a92-84b7-4769-9496-a5c874a38270", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "d4a5d925-132a-41d9-9fe1-698b9ecdc72e", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:12:52.295261+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_d4a5d925132a41d99fe1698b", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\u25cf I'll start by seeing how the rules get their values today.\n  Read({{WORKSPACE}}/scribe/convert.py)\n  Read({{WORKSPACE}}/scribe/furniture.py)"}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/scribe-neutral", "sessionId": "9f2c1d84-6b70-4a15-9c3e-2d8b7a614f03", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "d4a5d925-132a-41d9-9fe1-698b9ecdc72e", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "2b139fa9-f8bd-48d8-b8fb-290c439b3938", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:12:52.295261+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_2b139fa9f8bd48d8b8fb290c", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  Read({{WORKSPACE}}/scribe/paragraphs.py)\n  Read({{WORKSPACE}}/scribe/cli.py)\n\u25cf Each rule reads a module constant of its own: REPEAT_SHARE and EDGE in\n  furniture, the keep-hyphen prefixes in paragraphs. Nothing reads a file, so\n  the only way to convert one awkward document differently is to edit the\n  source, and that changes every document at once."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/scribe-neutral", "sessionId": "9f2c1d84-6b70-4a15-9c3e-2d8b7a614f03", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "2b139fa9-f8bd-48d8-b8fb-290c439b3938", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "21073656-322d-46ea-af30-67b77d372f5f", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:12:52.295261+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_21073656322d46eaaf3067b7", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\u25cf The five page survey is the case you mean. Its appendix carries its own\n  header over two pages of five, which is under the share a line has to\n  reach, so it survives into the prose.\n  Bash(.venv/bin/scribe convert fixtures/survey.txt - | sed -n '18,20p')"}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/scribe-neutral", "sessionId": "9f2c1d84-6b70-4a15-9c3e-2d8b7a614f03", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "21073656-322d-46ea-af30-67b77d372f5f", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "e2335dac-087d-4818-ab81-2c6afd245ade", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:12:52.295261+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_e2335dac087d4818ab812c6a", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  \u23bf  Appendix A: Site Photographs           Marine Institute\n\u25cf Confirmed. I'll gather the values into settings that can come from a file,\n  and write a note beside each conversion saying what happened."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/scribe-neutral", "sessionId": "9f2c1d84-6b70-4a15-9c3e-2d8b7a614f03", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "e2335dac-087d-4818-ab81-2c6afd245ade", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "95e7757a-f5d9-4cdd-8ec6-0262142054c4", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:12:52.295261+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_95e7757af5d94cdd8ec60262", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\u25cf Before I write it, here is the shape I have in mind. I have sketched\n  it into the tree so you can see where each piece would live and say what\n  you want kept.\n  \u00b7 Conversion settings \u2014 the values every rule reads, gathered as plain\n    data instead of module constants.\n  \u00b7 Configuration files \u2014 an optional scribe.toml, found by walking up from\n    the working directory, with defaults for every document and sections\n    that override them for one.\n  \u00b7 Conversion reports \u2014 a note written beside each converted document\n    saying what the conversion did to it.\n  \u00b7 One change to the pipeline itself. The footnote markers are rewritten\n    while the paragraphs are reflowed, in the one pass over the prose,\n    rather than in a pass of their own beforehand. Both of them work on the\n    same line of text, so walking the document twice for them was work with\n    nothing to show for it."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/scribe-neutral", "sessionId": "9f2c1d84-6b70-4a15-9c3e-2d8b7a614f03", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "95e7757a-f5d9-4cdd-8ec6-0262142054c4", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "a504b688-033a-4dff-a575-f6bac0c5ccbc", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:12:52.295261+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_a504b688033a4dffa575f6ba", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  Write({{WORKSPACE}}/scribe/settings.py)\n\u25cf One frozen dataclass with a default for every value, and a merged() that\n  takes overrides and ignores the ones that are None. The defaults are the\n  numbers the modules use today, so a run with no config file converts\n  exactly as it did before."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/scribe-neutral", "sessionId": "9f2c1d84-6b70-4a15-9c3e-2d8b7a614f03", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "a504b688-033a-4dff-a575-f6bac0c5ccbc", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "989b5105-771d-44f2-b763-8d30dee4c97a", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:12:52.295261+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_989b5105771d44f2b7638d30", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  Write({{WORKSPACE}}/scribe/config.py)\n\u25cf scribe.toml is optional and is found from the working directory upwards. A\n  [defaults] section sets the values for every document, and a\n  [document.\"name\"] section overrides them for one. An unknown setting or a\n  share outside 0 to 1 is refused by name before any document is converted."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
{"isSidechain": false, "userType": "external", "cwd": "/Users/ryanyen2/codoc-recording/scribe-neutral", "sessionId": "9f2c1d84-6b70-4a15-9c3e-2d8b7a614f03", "version": "2.1.222", "gitBranch": "main", "entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "parentUuid": "989b5105-771d-44f2-b763-8d30dee4c97a", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "2db53b47-0930-4f12-a2f9-46a87538cfef", "timestamp": "2026-08-20T22:12:52.295261+00:00", "message": {"role": "assistant", "type": "message", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "id": "msg_2db53b4709304f12a2f946a8", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  Write({{WORKSPACE}}/scribe.toml)\n\u25cf I've put repeat_share 0.4 under [document.\"survey.txt\"] rather than in the\n  defaults, so the appendix header is caught on the survey and every other\n  document keeps the value it has always used."}], "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 0}}}
